    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d759">

                <pb facs="0829" n="709" sameAs="frus:frus1931v02/pg709"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">411.12 Gomez and Robio/1: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Mexico</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Clark</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Mexico</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1931-06-08T18:00:00-06:00">June 8, 1931—6
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received 9:50 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>184. Reference killing of two Mexican youths in Ardmore, Oklahoma.</p>
                <p>Pursuant to telephone conversations between Johnson and Lane,<anchor n="10"
                        xml:id="d759-f1"/> I called on the President and Minister for Foreign
                    Affairs this afternoon, transmitted to each a copy of President’s Hoover’s
                    telegram to President Ortiz Rubio, and expressed the sincere regrets of the
                    Department and my own personal sympathy.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Clark</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d759-f1" n="10" xml:id="d759-f1-content">
                <p>Herschel V. Johnson, Chief of the Division of Mexican Affairs, Department of
                    State, and Arthur Bliss Lane, Counselor of Embassy in Mexico.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
